<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Deliberately almost empty, and the two absences are the point (PRD §12, SEC-1).

	  There is no `com.apple.security.app-sandbox`: the Accessibility API and a session event tap are
	  both refused inside the sandbox, and they are how the app reads a selection at all. The hardened
	  runtime is on instead (project.yml), which is what keeps library validation and the rest of it.

	  There is no `com.apple.security.automation.apple-events`: the app itself sends no Apple event.
	  M0 spike 3 measured the AppleScript route for reading a selection and it is not one of the
	  strategies the shipping chain uses. Extensions' AppleScripts run in PappuClipRunner.xpc, which
	  has the entitlement on its own (architecture §9.5); a bug here cannot drive another app.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<false/>
</dict>
</plist>
